    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d244-a4">

                <pb facs="0999" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg849"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Florence, Ariz.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H.
                        Kibbey</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Governor, Phoenix, Ariz</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your letter of
                    March 30, and will say in reply that I will do all in my power to detect and
                    prevent the sale of firearms to the Indians in this county, and further that I
                    will assist in any way possible in preventing arms from being sent from this
                    county to the Yaquis.</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James E. McGee</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sheriff</hi>.</signed><lb/>By <signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Wells</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Deputy</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
